{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794544784091,"sessionID":"ses_e2ccd29cbffeOwNLR1Qo8Fv8oA","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3344f1e0025lMSJpYHKmpUa1","sessionID":"ses_e2ccd29cbffeOwNLR1Qo8Fv8oA","messageID":"msg_1d33448c60015sNJdEybSwMuKX","type":"tool","id":"call_833b5653260d4f37b951d0c0","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md","offset":45,"limit":30},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 45-74\n45: ### Brief head form\n46: \n47: A recommendation that resolves to a command renders one label, shared by the `use` and `ambiguous` heads:\n48: \n49: ```text\n50: <ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)\n51: ```\n52: \n53: The recommendation's own `ownerSkillId`, `command` and `policy` are authoritative, and the generated command row fills only what they omit. The policy parenthesis is dropped when no policy is known. A recommendation with no command row keeps its skill label rather than a command label.\n54: \n55: The `use` head reads `Advisor: <freshness>; use <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` For example:\n56: \n57: ```text\n58: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n59: ```\n60: \n61: The ambiguous head applies the same label to both sides: `Advisor: <freshness>; ambiguous: <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> vs <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` Each label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`, so a control character, a line break or an instruction-shaped label renders nothing rather than reaching the model. The `Also:` line still names a doctor command by its runnable string.\n62: \n63: A hub whose compiled route defers or asks to clarify, and whose modes have commands, renders as `<hub> (needs a mode)` with no command, for example:\n64: \n65: ```text\n66: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.82/0.20 pass.\n67: ```\n68: \n69: The recommendation carries `needsMode: true`. A command on the same recommendation wins and the label is dropped.\n70: \n71: ### Degraded contract\n72: \n73: When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n74: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 75]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 45-74\n45: ### Brief head form\n46: \n47: A recommendation that resolves to a command renders one label, shared by the `use` and `ambiguous` heads:\n48: \n49: ```text\n50: <ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)\n51: ```\n52: \n53: The recommendation's own `ownerSkillId`, `command` and `policy` are authoritative, and the generated command row fills only what they omit. The policy parenthesis is dropped when no policy is known. A recommendation with no command row keeps its skill label rather than a command label.\n54: \n55: The `use` head reads `Advisor: <freshness>; use <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` For example:\n56: \n57: ```text\n58: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n59: ```\n60: \n61: The ambiguous head applies the same label to both sides: `Advisor: <freshness>; ambiguous: <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> vs <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` Each label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`, so a control character, a line break or an instruction-shaped label renders nothing rather than reaching the model. The `Also:` line still names a doctor command by its runnable string.\n62: \n63: A hub whose compiled route defers or asks to clarify, and whose modes have commands, renders as `<hub> (needs a mode)` with no command, for example:\n64: \n65: ```text\n66: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.82/0.20 pass.\n67: ```\n68: \n69: The recommendation carries `needsMode: true`. A command on the same recommendation wins and the label is dropped.\n70: \n71: ### Degraded contract\n72: \n73: When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n74: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 75]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\",\"offset\":45,\"limit\":30}"},"time":{"start":1794544783134,"end":1794544784091}}}}
